  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "Simplify \\[\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}}}.\\]",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\sqrt{x}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\sqrt[3]{x^2}\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\sqrt[27]{x^2}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\sqrt[54]{x}\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\sqrt[81]{x^{80}}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "The innermost square root requires \\(x\\ge 0\\). The useful observation is that \\(x\\sqrt{x}\\) is already a perfect cube:\n\\[\n(\\sqrt{x})^3=(\\sqrt{x})^2\\sqrt{x}=x\\sqrt{x}.\n\\]\nTherefore,\n\\[\n\\sqrt[3]{x\\sqrt{x}}=\\sqrt{x}.\n\\]\nStarting at the innermost cube root, this identity replaces that entire layer by \\(\\sqrt{x}\\). The middle layer then has the same form, and so does the outermost layer. Thus all three cube-root layers simplify in turn, leaving \\(\\boxed{\\sqrt{x}}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\). The argument includes \\(x=0\\).",
